Manual mode: one potentiometer rotates the base and another extends the arm. The buzzer warns me when an object gets within 8 cm.
Autonomous mode: the base sweeps while the sensor scans. When an object is within 20 cm, the arm picks it up, moves it to a drop zone, releases it, and returns home.
Skills I Gained
• Wiring circuits and reading pin diagrams
• Writing structured Arduino code with functions and state
• Controlling servos smoothly
• Measuring distance and handling bad sensor readings
• Debugging with the Serial Monitor and fixing real errors, such as an incomplete code paste and mixing up the 3-pin and 4-pin sensors
• Documenting a project with a README and sharing it on GitHub
Key Takeaway
Every robot follows the same loop: sense, decide, act. The sensors tell the controller what is happening, the controller decides, and the actuators move the world. This program let me build that loop from scratch, and the capstone put the whole thing together.
